      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "JSON::XS versions before 4.05 for Perl leak the decoded key of an object rejected for a missing colon in decode_hv.\n\nUnless it is short plain ASCII, a quoted key is decoded into a new scalar. Nothing frees that scalar when the object is rejected for a missing ':' after the key.\n\nA process that keeps running after a failed decode retains one key per rejected document, with its size chosen by the sender. Repeated requests exhaust process memory.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
